  "source_review": {
    "definition": "Minimum largest member among n distinct positive integers with all subset sums distinct. Retain15; add16 and17. No heuristic fingerprint is accepted as a certificate without exact collision resolution.",
    "primary_source": "Sol read Lunnon 1988 Integer Sets with Distinct Subset-Sums, DOI10.1090/S0025-5718-1988-0917837-5, Table1 w^2 column and formula(1.4). Published16 and17 maxima17072 and33531. Earlier provisional references17270 and34301 are weaker and archived separately. Reviewed newer Bohman general construction, whose limiting ratio does not by itself replace finite-size records. No stronger explicit finite source or optimality proof found in checked sources.",
    "human_baselines": "Conway-Guy recurrence yields17305 for16 and34301 for17. Same-parameter historical human methods reproduced independently of fixed best reference. Source lower bound from Dubroff-Fox-Xu binomial(n,floor(n/2)) gives12870 and24310, below the explicit constructions.",
    "independent_method": "Sol transcribed w2 values0,4,5,6,8,16,27,49,92,168,320,613,1177,2262,4432,8696,17072,33531 and independently reconstructed sorted w[n]-w[i] sets. Direct list doubling computes all65536 and131072 sums and checks exact distinctness, separate from the formal Gray-code checker. Human, reference, seed and search outputs all matched.",
    "admission": "All five strict programs, replay, cold export, corrupted witnesses, complete score-claim invariance and failure controls passed; original15 config preserved. Separate formal and human method scores retained."
  }
